So a terminating compiled program delivers its answer and certifies nothing. To certify a
claim about that answer, a target program must add a CHECK, a COMMIT and a CERTIFY;
this compiler does not insert that chain.

For clause independence, take one of the four witnesses in Theorem~\ref{thm:tc-independent}
and show that it also fails one of the three clauses it is said to meet, or that it meets
the clause it is said to fail. That would break the claimed independence witness.
